# Docs voice

Applies to DocFX markdown, `index.md`, root `README.md`, and packed `src/*/README.md`.
Keep/cut/rewrite lives in `DOC_USER_VOICE_PLAN.md` (DOC-00 table). Identity lives in
`LAWNDART_PRODUCT_POSITIONING.md`. Do not restate positioning. Do not re-derive voice.

## Zinsser

Strip every sentence. Cut words that do no work. Prefer short words and short
sentences. One idea when you can. Active verbs. Concrete nouns. No throat-clearing
and no decoration.

## Punctuation

No en dash (U+2013) and no em dash (U+2014). Use a period, comma, colon, or
parentheses. ASCII hyphen-minus only in compounds (`user-facing`) and in code.

## Lead and contrast

Lead with what is true and what to do. Do not open a page or section with a
negation. Contrast only when it adds information. One comparison is enough.

`docs/WHY.md` may compare Marten, Cratis, and Axon. It still leads with what
LawnDart is. No other page is a "not a..." list.

## Who owns which sentence

The line "LawnDart is the .NET runtime that event-modeled systems compile into"
stays on `README.md`, `index.md`, `docs/START_HERE.md`, `docs/OVERVIEW.md`, and
`docs/WHY.md`. Every other page starts with the topic.

CES count lives on `docs/CES_MATRIX.md`. Frozen surface lives on
`docs/DI_GRAMMAR.md`. `IProjector` is one glossary line if the type is still
public. Teaching pages author `ProjectionBase<TView>`.

## Competitors and plan voice

Marten, Cratis, Chronicle, Axon, EventStoreDB, and Kurrent appear only on
`docs/WHY.md` and `docs/LIBRARY_RAW_APPEND.md`. README links Why. It does not
name them.

No ticket ids, `Positioning §`, "reopened", "not a skill change", "do not split",
"Flywheel", `UseBoomerang`, or "Historical. Do not rename." Changelog may keep
history.

## What stays

Operational limits stay when the next sentence is the action (drop and recreate,
register the hop). Unused knobs stay omitted. Do not call them reserved.

"Do not" is for a footgun the reader will hit (`ThenThrows<DomainException>()`
vs wrapping `RunAsync` in `Assert.ThrowsAsync<InvalidOperationException>`).
Load through `GetOrCreateAsync` / `HandleCommandAsync`. Do not add a
`SetStreamId` warning. That method is `internal`.

Do not name a removed type except in `CHANGELOG.md`.

## Samples and code

Code is authority. Confirm types, headers, and status codes against `src/`.
HTTP maps `DomainException` to 422 and `ConcurrencyException` to 409.

Counter lives on README and Quickstart (`QuickstartCounterTests`). Library lives
on learning path 02-04, BDD, and the raw-append foil. Do not invent a third
domain. Excerpts must match the compiled slice.

```markdown
<!-- BAD -->
Do not look for those knobs. They do not exist.

<!-- GOOD -->
Snapshots are one row per stream. A write replaces that row.
```
